---
import '@fontsource-variable/fraunces';
import '@fontsource-variable/source-serif-4';

const title = 'Storya Consulting | AI for comms and publishing teams';
const description =
  'We look at how your comms or publishing team works, build the AI worth building, and keep it running. Paolo Danese and Rafael Soriano, Singapore.';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:title" content={title} />
    <meta property="og:description" content={description} />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://storyaconsulting.com" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://storyaconsulting.com" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main class="page">

      <header class="masthead">
        <div class="masthead__identity">
          <div class="masthead__portraits">
            <span class="portrait"><img src="/paolo-danese.jpg" alt="Paolo Danese" width="52" height="52"></span>
            <span class="portrait"><img src="/rafael-soriano.jpg" alt="Rafael Soriano" width="52" height="52"></span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="masthead__wordmark">Storya Consulting</p>
            <p class="masthead__byline">Paolo Danese &amp; Rafael Soriano · Singapore</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <hr class="rule-draw" aria-hidden="true">
      </header>

      <section class="hero" aria-label="Introduction">
        <p class="eyebrow">For PR, financial communications and publishing teams</p>
        <h1 class="hero__head">AI your team<br>still uses<br><em>a month later.</em></h1>
        <p class="hero__sub">We look at how work actually moves through your firm, build what's worth building with the people who will use it, and keep it running once it's live.</p>
        <ul class="doors">
          <li>
            <span class="doors__who">You haven't started, or what you tried didn't stick.</span>
            <a href="#look-first">Start with a workflow review</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="doors__who">Someone senior built a tool that works, and now they're stuck maintaining it.</span>
            <a href="#keep-it-running">Hand it over</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="why" aria-labelledby="why-head">
        <p class="section-num">01</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="why-head">Why none of it sticks</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">You've probably been offered AI training five times this year. On 16 September Singapore launched more than two hundred AI courses, and citizens who take one get six months of a premium AI tool. Plenty of people are learning. Far fewer firms have changed how the work gets done.</p>

        <div class="numerals">
          <figure class="num">
            <span class="num__digit">200+</span>
            <figcaption>AI courses launched on 16 September</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="num">
            <span class="num__digit">63%</span>
            <figcaption>of working-age people in Singapore used generative AI in early 2026</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="num num--accent">
            <span class="num__digit">3.8%</span>
            <figcaption>of firms have built AI into their core business processes</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>
        <p class="sources">SWDA, 16 September 2026 · Microsoft AI Diffusion Report, Q1 2026 · Ministry of Manpower, <em>Adoption of Artificial Intelligence Among Firms</em>, April 2026 (firms with 10 or more employees)</p>

        <div class="prose">
          <p>Something gets bought. People use it with one foot in and one foot out, and a year later there's a licence nobody opens and the work is done the old way.</p>
          <p>The most AI-advanced agency we've spoken to in this market did everything it was supposed to: a written AI policy, approved tools, a platform running dozens of agents, training taught by the CEO. We asked what was actually holding it back. The answer was culture, not technology. The hardest resistance sat with the directors, whose expertise was the thing clients paid for. And some staff were paying for a personal AI subscription out of their own pocket rather than use the licensed one on their desk.</p>
          <p>No course fixes that, because the course isn't the part that broke.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="columns">
          <div class="col">
            <h3 class="col__head">What a course gives you</h3>
            <ul class="list list--quiet">
              <li>A shared vocabulary</li>
              <li>Confidence with the tools</li>
              <li>A certificate</li>
              <li>Six months of a premium subscription</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="col col--accent">
            <h3 class="col__head">What's still missing the Monday after</h3>
            <ul class="list">
              <li>Which of your workflows is worth changing</li>
              <li>Something built on your own clients, documents and house style</li>
              <li>A written rule for what may go into which tool</li>
              <li>Someone who fixes it when it stops working</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="build" aria-labelledby="build-head">
        <p class="section-num">02</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="build-head">What we build</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">Small, specific tools that run every day inside work your team already does.</p>

        <div class="ba">
          <div class="ba__cell">
            <p class="ba__label">Before</p>
            <p class="ba__numeral">2<span class="unit">hrs</span></p>
            <p class="ba__body">Every morning, before anyone writes a word: press releases, regulators' websites, news feeds. The same two hours, every day, before the paid work starts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="ba__cell ba__cell--after">
            <p class="ba__label">After</p>
            <p class="ba__numeral">9<span class="unit">am</span></p>
            <p class="ba__body">The briefing is already done. Every claim links to the document and page it came from, and anything new since yesterday is flagged.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="subhead">The kind of thing that pays back fastest</h3>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>A style-guide check that catches house-style drift before an editor does.</li>
          <li>First drafts of coverage reports, built from the week's clippings and your own template.</li>
          <li>Release and Q&amp;A scaffolds that start from your past work.</li>
          <li>A research log that keeps what someone learned on an account after they move on.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="subhead">How we build</h3>
        <div class="grid6">
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">Sourced to the page.</h4>
            <p>Research output cites the document and page it came from. If a claim can't be traced, it doesn't ship.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">A review gate that can say no.</h4>
            <p>Nothing reaches a client without passing a defined check and a named person's sign-off.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">A data line, agreed first.</h4>
            <p>Before we build, we write down what may go into which tool. If your line is unpublished client material, we build so it can't reach a public model.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">Checkable without us.</h4>
            <p>Research ships with the source extracts and the exact prompt, so a sceptical editor can rerun it in their own account.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">On what you already pay for.</h4>
            <p>Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, ChatGPT, Claude or Gemini. You buy nothing new.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h4 class="grid6__head">Planned around your IT.</h4>
            <p>Corporate firewalls, device management, endpoint protection. We have fallbacks.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="look-first" aria-labelledby="look-head">
        <p class="section-num">03</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="look-head">Where the hours go</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">Before we recommend anything, we look at how work actually moves through your firm.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>What gets produced, by whom, how long it takes, and where the same job is being done four different ways by people who don't know about each other. We don't need a week of your team's time. We sit with one or two workflows from brief to delivery, talk to the people doing them, and follow the hours.</p>
        </div>
        <h3 class="subhead">What comes back is short</h3>
        <ul class="list">
          <li>A ranked list of places to intervene, each with what it costs to build and what it gives back. Where we can't put a number on something, we say so, and it goes lower down the list.</li>
          <li>The first thing we would build, and the things we would leave alone.</li>
          <li>A written data line: what may go into which tool, short enough that people follow it.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="priceline"><strong>SGD 5,000, fixed. Two to three weeks.</strong> Credited in full against a build if you go ahead within 60 days.</p>
        <p class="priceline priceline--guarantee">If the review doesn't find anything worth building, you don't pay for it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="adoption" aria-labelledby="adoption-head">
        <p class="section-num">04</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="adoption-head">The part that actually fails</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">A tool that gets bought and a tool that gets used are different things. The difference is whether the people who have to live with it want it.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>We start with the directors, before the team. The resistance that slows a firm down usually sits with the people whose judgement clients pay for, so they set the guardrails and approve what ships.</p>
          <p>Your people build part of it with us. By handover, whoever owns it can add a source, change a template or adjust an instruction without calling us.</p>
          <p>And we check whether it's being used. If it isn't, that is the finding, and we'd rather tell you in week three than discover it in month six.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="keep-it-running" aria-labelledby="run-head">
        <p class="section-num">05</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="run-head">Then we keep it running</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">AI tools drift. Models get retired, an API changes its terms, a prompt that worked in March does something odd in June, and the bill creeps up because nobody set a ceiling.</p>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>In most firms the person who notices is whoever built the thing, which usually means someone senior doing maintenance in the evenings. What happens to it when that person leaves?</p>
          <p>Everything we run is documented in plain English and lives on your accounts, so the knowledge stays with the firm.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div>
            <p class="steps__label">If we built it</p>
            <h3 class="steps__head">Monthly support</h3>
            <p>It picks up where the build's thirty days end: fixes when something changes underneath it, one improvement a month, and a monthly look at who's using it and who isn't.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="steps__label">If you built it</p>
            <h3 class="steps__head">A takeover</h3>
            <p>Some of the most useful AI tools in agencies were built by a founder or a director who got a prototype working and then got stuck keeping it alive. We review it, fix what will break first, set a cost ceiling and monitoring, and write the runbook. Then we keep it running, or hand it to your developer when you hire one.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="priceline"><strong>Takeover from SGD 5,000, fixed. Monthly support SGD 2,500.</strong> Hosting and API costs are billed to your own accounts, so there's no markup.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-head">
        <p class="section-num">06</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="pricing-head">What it costs</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">Less than you're bracing for, on purpose. Once this becomes a six-figure consulting engagement, it stops being something you can try. And if what we build doesn't do what we said it would, you don't pay for it. Prices in SGD. In person in Singapore; remote across the region.</p>
        <div class="tiers">
          <article class="tier tier--lead">
            <p class="tier__label">Look first</p>
            <h3 class="tier__name">Workflow review</h3>
            <p class="tier__price">SGD <span class="figure">5,000</span></p>
            <p class="tier__body">Two to three weeks on one or two of your workflows. A ranked list of where to intervene, with cost and return. Credited in full against a build within 60 days. No fee if it finds nothing worth building.</p>
            <a class="tier__cta" href="mailto:paolo@storyaconsulting.com?subject=Review">Email about a review</a>
          </article>
          <article class="tier">
            <p class="tier__label">Build</p>
            <h3 class="tier__name">One workflow, built with your team</h3>
            <p class="tier__price">From SGD <span class="figure">7,500</span></p>
            <p class="tier__body">Usually four to six weeks, on the tools you already pay for. Your people build part of it with us. Thirty days of support after handover. Half up front, half once it has run for thirty days doing what we agreed in writing. If it doesn't, we fix it at our cost, and if we can't, you don't pay the second half.</p>
            <a class="tier__cta" href="mailto:paolo@storyaconsulting.com?subject=Build">Email about a build</a>
          </article>
          <article class="tier">
            <p class="tier__label">Take over</p>
            <h3 class="tier__name">A tool you built yourselves</h3>
            <p class="tier__price">From SGD <span class="figure">5,000</span></p>
            <p class="tier__body">We review it, fix what will break first, set a cost ceiling and monitoring, and write the runbook nobody had time to write. Paid the same way as a build.</p>
            <a class="tier__cta" href="mailto:paolo@storyaconsulting.com?subject=Takeover">Email about a takeover</a>
          </article>
          <article class="tier">
            <p class="tier__label">Keep it running</p>
            <h3 class="tier__name">Monthly support</h3>
            <p class="tier__price">SGD <span class="figure">2,500</span><span class="cadence">/month</span></p>
            <p class="tier__body">Fixes when models or APIs change, one improvement a month, a monthly check on who's using it. Thirty days' notice to stop.</p>
            <a class="tier__cta" href="mailto:paolo@storyaconsulting.com?subject=Support">Email about support</a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="dont" aria-labelledby="dont-head">
        <p class="section-num">07</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="dont-head">What we don't do</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">Worth saying before you ask.</p>
        <p class="col__head stem">We don't</p>
        <div class="grid6">
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Run courses.</h3>
            <p>If your team needs a course, there are more than two hundred, and the government helps pay. We do the part after.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Certify compliance.</h3>
            <p>We don't write AI policies or audit you against a framework. We build workflows that won't create governance problems for whoever inherits them, and if you need a compliance adviser, we'll say so.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Lock you in.</h3>
            <p>What we build runs on your accounts and is documented well enough for someone else to take over.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Duplicate your developers.</h3>
            <p>If you already have people building, we fit around them. Working out where comes first.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Stay forever.</h3>
            <p>Most agencies can't yet justify a full-time AI lead. We can be the step before that hire, and help write the job description when it's time.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="grid6__head">Build for the sake of it.</h3>
            <p>Some workflows aren't worth automating. When that's the answer, the review says so.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="videos" aria-labelledby="videos-head">
        <p class="section-num">08</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="videos-head">Dumb Questions About AI</h2>
        <p class="section-deck">A short weekly video series for people in PR and communications. Rafael asks the questions everyone in the room is too senior to ask out loud. Paolo answers them.</p>
        <ol class="episodes">
          <li>
            <a class="ep" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paolodanese_in-collab-with-rafael-p-soriano-we-will-be-ugcPost-7501119793627029504-qA8r/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="ep__num">01</span>
              <span class="ep__title">Can I put a client's unpublished announcement into ChatGPT?</span>
              <span class="ep__meta">Watch</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="ep" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paolodanese_and-here-is-the-second-episode-of-our-dumb-ugcPost-7503729282951696384-_3vA/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="ep__num">02</span>
              <span class="ep__title">What am I actually paying for?</span>
              <span class="ep__meta">Watch</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <a class="ep" href="https://www.linkedin.com/posts/paolodanese_here-we-are-with-the-latest-episode-of-dumb-ugcPost-7506222654949875712-FKe8/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
              <span class="ep__num">03</span>
              <span class="ep__title">Why is every answer from chatbots different, even with the same question?</span>
              <span class="ep__meta">Watch</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <div class="ep">
              <span class="ep__num">04</span>
              <span class="ep__title">My team says they use AI. Why hasn't anything got faster?</span>
              <span class="ep__meta">Out next</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="after-list">A new episode every week on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/paolodanese/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="who" aria-labelledby="who-head">
        <p class="section-num">09</p>
        <h2 class="section-head" id="who-head">Who's behind this</h2>
        <div class="bios">
          <div>
            <div class="bio__photo"><img src="/paolo-danese.jpg" alt="Paolo Danese" width="480" height="600"></div>
            <h3 class="bio__name">Paolo Danese</h3>
            <p class="bio__body">Paolo Danese founded <strong>Storya</strong>, an AI publishing platform that grew to 3,000 users and 1,000 independent authors across more than 20 languages before it was wound down in 2023. Much of what he knows about building AI that people keep using comes from that, including the parts that didn't work. Before Storya he spent close to a decade as a financial journalist at <strong>Euromoney Institutional Investor</strong>, where he ran <em>GlobalRMB</em>, the first English-language publication covering China's currency internationalisation, and then led content and media relations for institutional finance clients as a <strong>VP at FleishmanHillard</strong> in Hong Kong. He has published five epic fantasy novels and runs an AI agent that manages the Amazon Ads on them.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="bio__photo"><img src="/rafael-soriano.jpg" alt="Rafael Soriano" width="480" height="600"></div>
            <h3 class="bio__name">Rafael Soriano</h3>
            <p class="bio__body">Rafael Soriano leads partnerships and the adoption side of Storya Consulting's work: getting the people who have to live with a new tool to want it. Rafael has spent more than twenty years getting organisations with different agendas to agree on something and then act on it, through corporate innovation programmes, public-private partnerships and cross-border alliances in Singapore, Asia-Pacific and the United States. For the <strong>Association for Financial Professionals</strong>, that meant building a network of seven financial institutions across seven Southeast Asian markets, which brought in a tenth of the association's Asia-Pacific sales within eight months. In 2024 Rafael co-founded <strong>Akitsu Consulting</strong>, where the work includes integrating international professional standards into Singapore's SkillsFuture framework with NTUC LearningHub. Before any of that, Rafael spent four years as a police officer in Kansas City, a job built on de-escalation and mediation. MBA, <strong>Johns Hopkins</strong>.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="cta" aria-label="Get in touch">
        <p class="cta__line">Bring what you've tried.</p>
        <p class="cta__line cta__line--accent">And what didn't stick.</p>
        <p class="cta__sub">Twenty minutes, over coffee in Singapore or on a call. If we're not useful, you'll know inside the first ten.</p>
        <a class="cta__email" href="mailto:paolo@storyaconsulting.com">paolo@storyaconsulting.com</a>
      </section>

      <footer class="foot">
        <div class="foot__row">
          <p>Storya Consulting · Singapore · 2026</p>
          <p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/paolodanese/" target="_blank" rel="me noopener">Paolo on LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/rafaelpsorianomba/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rafael on LinkedIn</a></p>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </main>

    <style is:global>
      /* Tokens: light palette is the live site's own (index.astro). Dark is a considered counterpart. */
      :root {
        --paper: oklch(98% 0.008 75);
        --paper-2: oklch(95.5% 0.013 75);
        --ink: oklch(18% 0.02 50);
        --ink-soft: oklch(34% 0.018 55);
        --ink-mute: oklch(52% 0.015 60);
        --rule: oklch(82% 0.012 60);
        --accent: oklch(48% 0.16 28);
        --accent-ink: oklch(98% 0.008 75);
        --max: 1100px;
        --prose: 38rem;
        --display: 'Fraunces Variable', 'Fraunces', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        --body: 'Source Serif 4 Variable', 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;
        color-scheme: light;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
          --paper: oklch(17.5% 0.012 55);
          --paper-2: oklch(21.5% 0.014 55);
          --ink: oklch(94% 0.012 75);
          --ink-soft: oklch(83% 0.014 70);
          --ink-mute: oklch(68% 0.014 65);
          --rule: oklch(34% 0.014 55);
          --accent: oklch(71% 0.14 36);
          --accent-ink: oklch(17.5% 0.012 55);
          color-scheme: dark;
        }
      }
      :root[data-theme="dark"] {
        --paper: oklch(17.5% 0.012 55);
        --paper-2: oklch(21.5% 0.014 55);
        --ink: oklch(94% 0.012 75);
        --ink-soft: oklch(83% 0.014 70);
        --ink-mute: oklch(68% 0.014 65);
        --rule: oklch(34% 0.014 55);
        --accent: oklch(71% 0.14 36);
        --accent-ink: oklch(17.5% 0.012 55);
        color-scheme: dark;
      }

      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body {
        margin: 0;
        background: var(--paper);
        color: var(--ink);
        font-family: var(--body);
        font-size: 17px;
        line-height: 1.55;
        font-feature-settings: 'kern', 'liga';
        -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
        text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
      }
      ::selection { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); }
      a { color: var(--ink); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); transition: border-color .2s, color .2s; }
      a:hover { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }
      a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 3px; border-radius: 2px; }
      h1, h2, h3 { text-wrap: balance; }

      /* Page frame */
      .page {
        max-width: var(--max);
        margin-inline: auto;
        padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        padding-block: 2.25rem 4rem;
      }

      /* Masthead */
      .masthead__identity { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; }
      .masthead__portraits { display: flex; }
      .portrait {
        display: block;
        width: 52px;
        height: 52px;
        border-radius: 999px;
        overflow: hidden;
        background: var(--paper-2);
        border: 2px solid var(--paper);
        flex: none;
      }
      .portrait + .portrait { margin-left: -12px; }
      .portrait img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: 50% 0%;
        transform: scale(1.7);
        transform-origin: 50% 38%;
      }
      .masthead__wordmark {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 600;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36, 'SOFT' 0;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        margin: 0;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .masthead__byline { margin: .15rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-mute); font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
      .rule-draw {
        border: 0;
        height: 2px;
        margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
        background: var(--accent);
        transform-origin: left center;
        animation: ruleDraw 700ms cubic-bezier(.22, 1, .36, 1) 150ms both;
      }
      @keyframes ruleDraw { from { transform: scaleX(0); } to { transform: scaleX(1); } }

      /* Sections */
      section { padding-block: 4.5rem; }
      section + section { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .section-num {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        color: var(--accent);
        font-size: .82rem;
        letter-spacing: .22em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        margin: 0 0 .9rem;
      }
      .section-head {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 480;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 96;
        font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 4vw, 2.6rem);
        line-height: 1.05;
        letter-spacing: -0.018em;
        margin: 0 0 .8rem;
      }
      .section-deck { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.08rem; max-width: var(--prose); margin: 0 0 2.4rem; }
      .prose p { max-width: var(--prose); margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
      .prose p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
      .subhead {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 520;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
        font-size: .95rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
        margin: 3rem 0 1rem;
      }
      .priceline {
        margin: 2.2rem 0 0;
        padding-top: 1.2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        max-width: var(--prose);
        color: var(--ink-soft);
      }
      .priceline--guarantee { margin-top: 0.5rem; padding-top: 0; border-top: 0; }
      .priceline strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }

      /* Hero */
      .hero { padding-block: 4.5rem 5rem; }
      .eyebrow {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 500;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .22em;
        font-size: .78rem;
        color: var(--accent);
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
      }
      .hero__head {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 420;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 30;
        font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5.2rem);
        line-height: .98;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        max-width: 18ch;
      }
      .hero__head em {
        font-style: italic;
        font-weight: 360;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1;
        color: var(--accent);
      }
      .hero__sub { font-size: 1.18rem; line-height: 1.5; max-width: var(--prose); margin: 0 0 2.4rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
      .doors { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .doors li { padding-block: 1.1rem 1.25rem; padding-inline: 0 1.5rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: .55rem; }
      .doors li + li { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-inline: 1.5rem 0; }
      .doors__who { color: var(--ink-soft); }
      .doors a {
        align-self: flex-start;
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 560;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        font-size: .78rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
        padding-bottom: 2px;
      }

      /* Numerals */
      .numerals {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        gap: 2rem;
        margin: 1.4rem 0 .9rem;
        padding-block: 2rem;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
        border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
      }
      .num { margin: 0; }
      .num__digit {
        display: block;
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 380;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 0;
        font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 8.5vw, 7rem);
        line-height: .9;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        font-variant-numeric: lining-nums;
      }
      .num--accent .num__digit { color: var(--accent); }
      .num figcaption { color: var(--ink-soft); margin-top: .6rem; max-width: 24ch; line-height: 1.4; font-size: .98rem; }
      .sources { margin: 0 0 3rem; font-size: .84rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-mute); max-width: 60rem; }

      /* Two columns */
      .columns { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; margin-top: 3rem; }
      .col__head {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 520;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
        font-size: .95rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
      }
      .col--accent .col__head { color: var(--accent); }
      .list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
      .list li { padding-block: .85rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .list li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .list--quiet li { color: var(--ink-mute); }

      /* Before / after */
      .ba { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .ba__cell { padding: 2.2rem 2rem 2.4rem 0; }
      .ba__cell + .ba__cell { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-inline: 2rem 0; }
      .ba__label {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 540;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .22em;
        font-size: .78rem;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
        margin: 0 0 .5rem;
      }
      .ba__cell--after .ba__label, .ba__cell--after .ba__numeral { color: var(--accent); }
      .ba__numeral {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 380;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 0;
        font-size: clamp(3.6rem, 8vw, 6.5rem);
        line-height: 1;
        margin: 0 0 .8rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.035em;
      }
      .ba__numeral .unit { font-size: .32em; font-weight: 460; margin-left: .3em; color: var(--ink-mute); letter-spacing: 0; }
      .ba__body { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 34ch; }

      /* Six-cell grids */
      .grid6 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 2.4rem; }
      .grid6__head {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 480;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
        font-size: 1.18rem;
        margin: 0 0 .5rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      }
      .grid6 p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }
      .stem { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }

      /* Two steps */
      .steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; margin-top: 2.6rem; }
      .steps__label {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 540;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .22em;
        font-size: .78rem;
        color: var(--accent);
        margin: 0 0 .5rem;
      }
      .steps__head {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 460;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 48;
        font-size: 1.6rem;
        margin: 0 0 .6rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.014em;
      }
      .steps p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }

      /* Pricing */
      .tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .tier { padding: 2rem 1.5rem 2.2rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      .tier:first-child { padding-left: 0; }
      .tier + .tier { border-left: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .tier__label {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 540;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .22em;
        font-size: .76rem;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
        margin: 0 0 .5rem;
      }
      .tier__name {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 460;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.2;
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        letter-spacing: -0.012em;
      }
      .tier__price {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 460;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 14;
        font-size: .8rem;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
      }
      .tier__price .figure {
        display: inline-block;
        font-weight: 380;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144;
        font-size: 2.7rem;
        line-height: 1;
        letter-spacing: -0.03em;
        color: var(--ink);
        text-transform: none;
        margin-inline: .12em;
        font-variant-numeric: lining-nums tabular-nums;
      }
      .tier__price .cadence { font-size: .8rem; text-transform: lowercase; letter-spacing: .04em; }
      .tier--lead .tier__label, .tier--lead .tier__price .figure { color: var(--accent); }
      .tier__body { margin: 0 0 1.6rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .97rem; flex: 1; }
      .tier__cta {
        align-self: flex-start;
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 540;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        font-size: .74rem;
        border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor;
        padding-bottom: 2px;
      }

      /* Episodes: each published episode's whole row is its link */
      .episodes { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .episodes li { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
      .ep {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 3rem 1fr auto;
        gap: .4rem 1rem;
        align-items: baseline;
        padding-block: 1rem;
      }
      a.ep { border-bottom: 0; }
      .ep__num { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 520; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: .12em; font-size: .85rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
      .ep__title { font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 460; font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36; font-size: 1.22rem; line-height: 1.25; }
      .ep__meta {
        justify-self: start;
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 520;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: .16em;
        font-size: .72rem;
        color: var(--ink-mute);
        white-space: nowrap;
      }
      a.ep .ep__meta { color: var(--ink); border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; padding-bottom: 2px; }
      a.ep:hover .ep__meta { color: var(--accent); }
      .after-list { margin: 1.4rem 0 0; color: var(--ink-soft); }

      /* Bios */
      .bios { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
      .bio__photo {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 240px;
        aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
        overflow: hidden;
        border-radius: 2px;
        background: var(--paper-2);
        margin: 0 0 1.3rem;
      }
      .bio__photo img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: 50% 0%;
        transform: scale(1.2);
        transform-origin: 50% 30%;
      }
      .bio__name {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 480;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36;
        font-size: 1.35rem;
        margin: 0 0 .7rem;
      }
      .bio__body { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.65; }
      .bio__body strong { font-weight: 600; }

      /* Closing */
      .cta { padding-block: 6rem 5rem; }
      .cta__line {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 380;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 6.2vw, 4.4rem);
        line-height: 1;
        margin: 0;
        letter-spacing: -0.025em;
      }
      .cta__line--accent {
        color: var(--accent);
        font-style: italic;
        font-weight: 360;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 144, 'SOFT' 100, 'WONK' 1;
      }
      .cta__sub { margin: 1.6rem 0 1.2rem; color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: var(--prose); }
      .cta__email {
        font-family: var(--display);
        font-weight: 480;
        font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 36;
        font-size: 1.4rem;
        border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);
        padding-bottom: 3px;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
      }

      /* Footer */
      .foot { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 1rem; padding-top: 1.4rem; }
      .foot__row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: space-between; gap: .6rem 1.5rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--ink-mute); }
      .foot__row p { margin: 0; }
      .foot__row a { color: var(--ink-mute); border-bottom-color: transparent; }
      .foot__row a:hover { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

      /* Narrow screens */
      @media (max-width: 980px) {
        .tiers { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
        .tier:nth-child(3) { border-left: 0; padding-left: 0; }
        .tier:nth-child(n+3) { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
        .grid6 { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      }
      @media (max-width: 720px) {
        .doors, .numerals, .columns, .ba, .steps, .bios { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .doors li + li { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-inline: 0; }
        .numerals { gap: 1.4rem; }
        .num figcaption { max-width: none; }
        .ba__cell { padding-inline: 0; }
        .ba__cell + .ba__cell { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-inline: 0; }
        .columns, .steps { gap: 2rem; }
      }
      @media (max-width: 600px) {
        .tiers, .grid6 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
        .tier { padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0; }
        .tier + .tier { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
        .grid6 { gap: 1.6rem; }
        .ep { grid-template-columns: 2.2rem 1fr; }
        .ep__meta { grid-column: 2; }
      }
      @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
        .rule-draw { animation: none; }
        a { transition: none; }
      }
    </style>
  </body>
</html>
